# Counterfactual: a hostile reader of the contribution record added
#
# The constitution plus one rule that conditions confinement on the absence of
# a contribution record. The engine accepts it — pay is a base relation, so
# there is no negative cycle for the stratifier to refuse — and it derives.
# This is the measured defect the repository guard on `pay` exists to close,
# and this fixture is that guard's watched failing control: the guard must
# reject this copy and accept the real constitution.
:expect-pins 4
# Nobody in the cast holds a contribution record, so the rule confines every
# registered person at once.
? prisoner(Bela).
# => TRUE
? prisoner(Cira).
# => TRUE
# A record at the named scheme is the only way out — the work-conditioning of
# liberty this design refuses.
pay(Bela, Contribution, Carrier, SchemeA).
? prisoner(Bela).
# => FALSE
# The floor itself is still not read by the hostile rule.
? entitled(Cira, event { eats() }).
# => TRUE
